      "key": {
        "uuid": "264bb932_d10d0f31",
        "filename": "libartservice/service/java/com/android/server/art/PreRebootDexoptJob.java",
        "patchSetId": 13
      },
      "lineNbr": 396,
      "author": {
        "id": 1373864
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-02-14T15:04:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ah, this requires the synchronization monitor. That\u0027s unfortunate, but I think this check is valuable enough from a readability perspective, especially given that `triggerUpdateEnginePostinstallAndWait` has a nontrivial return flow.\n\nGood to see the `mCancellationSignal.isCanceled()` condition as well. I suggest returning if that is true before doing this check. Then the reader doesn\u0027t have to wonder what `run` might do for an already cancelled job.\n\nThat leads to the question whether we want to report stats if the job is cancelled this early. I don\u0027t think that\u0027s a given - we could view it as that update_engine changed its mind and didn\u0027t want us to do anything after all, and we also haven\u0027t spent any noticeable effort so far, so it seems fair to act as if it never happened.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 396,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 396,
        "endChar": 90
      },
      "revId": "ac41478269a68855a7506eb6126f87ee3bd03c57",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "68d1fd2e_76a5ac16",
        "filename": "libartservice/service/java/com/android/server/art/PreRebootDexoptJob.java",
        "patchSetId": 13
      },
      "lineNbr": 396,
      "author": {
        "id": 1884045
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-02-14T22:53:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Alright, added an early return. I\u0027m not a fan of inessential code because people may thought it must be there and be hesitant when they want to change it, just like how we hesitanted many times when we were porting the legacy code and saw code that didn\u0027t look essential. However, saving people time on tracing into a function may be a good reason for it. I added a comment to mitigate my concern.\n\nI do think the stats reporting is necessary. At this point, `mCancellationSignal` is likely fired by the job scheduler through `onStopJob` -\u003e `onStopJobImpl` -\u003e `cancelGivenLocked`, not by update_engine (because we were just notified by update_engine a blink ago). In this case, we do want to know why the job scheduler changed its mind so quickly.",
      "parentUuid": "264bb932_d10d0f31",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 396,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 396,
        "endChar": 90
      },
      "revId": "ac41478269a68855a7506eb6126f87ee3bd03c57",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ecb228cf_49d6d483",
        "filename": "libartservice/service/java/com/android/server/art/PreRebootDexoptJob.java",
        "patchSetId": 13
      },
      "lineNbr": 396,
      "author": {
        "id": 1373864
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-02-17T18:41:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e people may thought it must be there and be hesitant when they want to change it\n\nActually, they should be. When that time comes there may be code in `run` that (perhaps inadvertently) depends on this return, regardless of what a comment might claim. Personally I wouldn\u0027t trust it.\n\nEven so, \"unnecessarily\" returning early on cancel outweighs that imo, also because it follows the principle of least surprise.\n\n\u003e In this case, we do want to know why the job scheduler changed its mind so quickly.\n\nI see, good point.",
      "parentUuid": "68d1fd2e_76a5ac16",
